// E0002 for `when` and `reset_if` written as the name of a flow input and read in the body (S-1082, S-654, §2.3), as
// `keyword_name_param_used.onsa` for `in`. The candidate is `when_` at the input only. The `when` of the body is the
// error of the unit after that (an expression, where it cannot start one: no postfix clause, no expression before it
// on its line or the line before), with the same candidate: the fix takes two steps, and the diagnostic that is left
// after the first is the second step (`leaves`). One error in each unit.

pub flow fw(when: F32 at sample) -> F32 at sample { //~ E0002
  when
}

pub flow fr(reset_if: F32 at sample) -> F32 at sample {   //~ E0002
  reset_if
}
